Most those troubles can be avoided by other methods or arn't that bad in 
the late game, and arn't that common in the early game. A good ascendable 
character should include all the normal resistances, a ring of free 
action, and boots of speed. I believe that leaves level drain, sticking 
(eg. mimics), lycanthropy, energy drain, slime, and disenchanting as the 
only problems. A few of those (energy drain, sticking) are not worth 
worrying about. Lycanthropy and Disenchanting can be bad, but require you  
to be hit by a weak monster, which is your own fault in the late game. 
Level drain can easily be avoided with the right weapon, but also isn't a 
problem in the late game, if you get level drained just kill what drained 
you and get back to your starting level, you'll lose some experience but 
few people expect to gain levels from experience once they hit XL 15+. 
Slime is probably the worst of the bunch, but any source of fire will 
undo the effects, and you really should kill a Green Slime before it gets 
that close anyway.

